            "title": "Group records into lines",
            "detail": "Per patient, by start date: a record starting more than 90 days after every earlier one has stopped begins a new line; anything closer — overlapping, or a switch within the gap — is the same line. A line is named by its sorted combination of classes ('A + B'); the label never decides which records form a line."
